mw2coop patch for maps/_slowmo_breach.gsc (Modern Warfare 2, 64-bit Steam build)

1. The breach hint sits 43 units higher in the console's split screen (-23 instead of 20). The native split
   screen on one machine is that layout, but the game's IsSplitScreen() is false there: the mod's dvar
   mw2coop_native_split (set while the picture is split) stands in for it.
@@@ replace
	hint_offset = 20;
	if ( issplitscreen() )
		hint_offset = -23;
@@@ with
	hint_offset = 20;
	if ( issplitscreen() || GetDvarInt( "mw2coop_native_split" ) )
		hint_offset = -23;
@@@ end

2. After the breach a player let go inside the door's or the charge's collision cannot move (owner, 2026-11-16, Just Like Old Times: "one of the players stays
   stuck at the door after the breach"): a player who cannot take a step is put next to the other one once that one stands on free ground.
@@@ replace
		else
		{
			player Unlink();
		}

		player Show();
	}
@@@ with
		else
		{
			player Unlink();
		}

		player Show();
	}
	if ( maps\_mw2coop::is_campaign_coop() && isdefined( level.player2 ) )
		level thread maps\_mw2coop::breach_unstick( self.origin, ent.room_volume.origin );
@@@ end

3. A breach whose door was already blown (a later start point, a co-op restart at a checkpoint after it) has no lookat trigger any more: the
   objectives' assign_script_breachgroup_to_ents() read its breach origin as undefined, a script error that ended the objectives for the rest
   of the level (night tour 2026-11-18: Loose Ends restarted at house_briefing). Such a trigger is passed by.
@@@ replace
				if ( distance( ent.origin, trigger.breach_origin ) > 80 )
@@@ with
				if ( !isdefined( trigger ) || !isdefined( trigger.breach_origin ) || distance( ent.origin, trigger.breach_origin ) > 80 )
@@@ end
